          "pause": true,
          "displayType": "poster",
          "buttonOnMobile": false,
          "label": "<p>The video argues that de-escalation to targeted therapy — the most important ste</p>",
          "x": 30,
          "y": 30,
          "width": 40,
          "height": 25,
          "libraryTitle": "Multiple Choice",
          "action": {
            "library": "H5P.MultiChoice 1.16",
            "params": {
              "question": "<p>The video argues that de-escalation to targeted therapy — the most important stewardship strategy — can only succeed if one prerequisite step happens before the very first antibiotic dose. What is that prerequisite?</p>",
              "answers": [
                {
                  "text": "<div>Formulary restriction on carbapenems and colistin</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Restricting last-resort drugs protects them for later, but it does not by itself enable de-escalation — that requires knowing the causative organism's susceptibility first.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Sending cultures for microbiological testing</div>",
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Correct. Without a culture sent before the first dose, there is no susceptibility data to de-escalate against later — this is why the video calls specimen collection the true foundation of stewardship.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Starting broad-spectrum empirical therapy immediately</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Empirical therapy is often necessary while awaiting results, but starting it is not the prerequisite that enables de-escalation — sending the culture beforehand is.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Ordering a procalcitonin biomarker level</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Procalcitonin and other rapid diagnostics help speed up decisions, but the video identifies culture collection before the first dose as the essential foundation, not biomarker testing.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                }
              ],
              "overallFeedback": [
                {
                  "from": 0,
                  "to": 50,
                  "feedback": "Re-examine the stewardship hierarchy: de-escalation only works if a culture was sent before empirical therapy began, making specimen collection the true foundation of the whole programme."
                },
                {
                  "from": 51,
                  "to": 100,
                  "feedback": "Correct — sending cultures before the first antibiotic dose is the foundation that makes later de-escalation possible."
                }
              ],
